This repository contains the source code of the Dragon's Dogma 2 Trainer Claude Companion ("the Software"), an
optional add-on for the Dragon's Dogma 2 Trainer by RipXic. The source is published so that anyone can read it, check
what it does, and run it for themselves. It is NOT open source.

1. What you MAY do
   a. Read and study the source code.
   b. Run the Software on your own computer, for your own single-player use.
   c. Make changes for your own private, personal use, as long as you never share the changed version (see 2).
   d. Link to this repository or to the official download page:
      https://github.com/RipXic/DragonsDogma2TrainerClaudeCompanion/releases

2. What you may NOT do without written permission from RipXic
   a. Redistribute, re-upload, mirror or share the Software, its source code, or any part of it, on any website, mod
      site, file host, launcher, mod pack, collection, Discord server or anywhere else.
   b. Publish or distribute modified versions, forks, ports or derivative works (including "fixed", "updated",
      translated or re-branded versions).
   c. Use the Software, its source code or any part of it in another product, trainer, tool or project.
   d. Sell, rent, license or otherwise make money from the Software or anything built from it, including putting it
      behind a paywall, subscription or "early access".
   e. Remove or change this license, the copyright notice, or the credits.
   f. Use the Software in online / multiplayer sessions to gain an advantage over other players.
   g. Use the Software, its source code or any part of it to train, fine-tune, evaluate or build datasets for
      artificial intelligence or machine-learning models or code assistants, or feed it to an AI tool in order to
      produce a copy, port, rewrite or derivative of it for distribution. This applies to people and to automated
      systems (crawlers, scrapers, AI agents) alike. Reading the code with an AI tool for your own private
      understanding or your own private use (section 1) is allowed; publishing anything produced that way is not.
      (The Software's own "Ask Claude" feature, used as intended, is not affected by this point.)

3. GitHub
   When this repository is public on GitHub, GitHub's Terms of Service allow GitHub users to view and fork public
   repositories on GitHub itself; that permission exists only as far as GitHub's terms require it. A fork does not
   grant any of the rights withheld in section 2: you may not distribute, release or publish versions from a fork.

4. Third-party code
   The Software contains no third-party code. It runs on Windows PowerShell (part of Windows) and, for the optional
   "Ask Claude" feature, starts the Claude Code program that comes with the Claude desktop app, which you install
   yourself under its own terms. This license covers everything in this repository.

5. No warranty
   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Use it at your own risk and keep your own backups.
   The author is not liable for any damage, data loss, costs on your Claude plan, bans or other problems that come
   from using it.

6. Not affiliated
   The Dragon's Dogma 2 Trainer and this companion are fan-made tools. They are not affiliated with, endorsed by or
   connected to Capcom or Anthropic. Dragon's Dogma and its content belong to Capcom; Claude belongs to Anthropic.

If you want to do something that section 2 does not allow (for example host it on another site, or use part of the
code), ask RipXic through the GitHub repository above (open an issue). Permission only counts if it is given in writing.
